cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Ogrow: perfusion-limited growth of vascularised tissue from one nucleation
  law
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software and
  the paper it belongs to.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A generative model in which liver-like, kidney-like and pancreas-like
  constructs grow from the same local rules on a perfused vascular tree: a
  functional unit forms at a tip at a rate set by the competent cells held
  there and by the excess of local perfusion over a setpoint, bounded by
  perfusion per unit, by competent cells and by room. Three growth regimes
  follow from one binary property of the cell source, whether the cell that
  forms a unit is spent in forming it. The repository regenerates every number
  and figure of the accompanying manuscript with `make paper`, and checks the
  manuscript against the results it quotes.
